{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head bd87e619aa990c183a32647c55cdeb108a615650, on planner/act-env-sixth-20261116, its one artifact `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md`, for request 54bedd4c under my promise bd82800a. This verdict names the one implementation: the sixth amendment (request 5f15823c, promise 35370d96). Main cfe769ce is the parent, and the diff is that one file, 114 lines added and 13 removed. The head lands after the E4, A1 and CR-2 head f7208649.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- Section 6. The two forms of a return match ruling ff578fef and its correction 481aac4e. A return by an exploration holds the reason, the changed fields and `now`. A return by a refused or withdrawn request holds the exact cause, no `now`, and its kept basis. The race at heads 39 and 40 uses the cause that 481aac4e gives, an ordinary race and no fault of a replica. The rule that only a call of the member changes a draft, the `other-recorded` rule with `restore(key)` and `dismiss(key)` (fc765743), the one required draft store, and the rule that a call owns its inputs before its first wait (bbee5700) match their rulings.\n- Section 6.1. The optional item field, the edit as a patch, and `clear(slot, fields)` match ruling c1b26daf item by item.\n- Section 15. The rule-5 row now names both forms. The new row records the change of D12 section 8 for `other-recorded`. The paragraph \"A call reports what the store holds\" matches bbee5700 item 3.\n- Section 19 adds four rows for the five rulings, and the opening paragraph names 16 November.\n\nThe planner's three questions:\n\n1. One other passage still describes a single return. Section 10, problem 3 of the field table (line 1008), says that the draft \"returns one time with the reason and the changed field\". In the race of section 6 the draft returns twice: first with the cause, then with `now`. Correct that row in the next amendment. No other section promises `now` for a refusal. Line 565 and section 6.1 speak of an exploration, and line 1281 records the owner's earlier decision as history.\n2. Rule 4 now names only the drafts that rule 3 returned. The new paragraph covers the second form: a submit explores first, and an unchanged basis makes a new version on the kept basis. That keeps \"the only way that a step gets a new basis\" true, because the second form keeps its basis. A basis that `clear` captures for a newly selected subject is a first capture under section 6.1, and it gives no step a new basis.\n3. The section 15 table is where this note records each change to D12, as the earlier amendments did. A row there is enough, as long as the client note stays the earlier design and this note governs C4.\n\nChecks: `check-notes.mjs cfe769ce bd87e619` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links.mjs` exits 0, the commit-message check passes with 1 checked and 0 flagged, and `git diff --check` is clean. Under the notes-only ruling, I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The second form keeps a refusal a projection of the custody record, so no background step writes the draft store, and two clients of one member cannot race on a return. One required draft store replaces the C3 stand-in, so a page has one option to supply.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The client never signs on a basis that the member did not see. A refusal does not move the basis, and the next submit explores before it signs. `restore` makes the member choose a second submit of an act that makes a new item, so no view repeats a creation.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One rule serves both `other-recorded` cases, an empty slot and a slot that holds another draft.\n\nQualifications that stand: this is a design note, and C4 has built none of these rules yet. The how-to page of C4 owes the race case, the `undefined` rule and the write column for `state` and `taken`. This approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing, after f7208649.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e01bddd5f016fffe4d8d84d78ec43bfd134c14d9","binding":"assigned","head":"bd87e619aa990c183a32647c55cdeb108a615650","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bd82800af81181ab26d6124ea002d19afced757b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:35370d9609a3b652acb706f97c8c56e604c509da\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bd82800af81181ab26d6124ea002d19afced757b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}